# ── Large derived data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All of these regenerate from the delivered source plus the code in datagen/.
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments -- "path # note" is a literal pattern.
#
# multimodal_trajectories_v1.csv is 111 MB. GitHub's per-file hard limit is 100 MB,
# so committing it does not fail at review time, it fails at push time.
# Regenerate: sbatch/run_exec_trajectories.sbatch with RUN_EXPORT=true
data/multimodal_trajectories_v1.csv
# 37 MB. Regenerate: datagen/export_rendered_items.py
data/multimodal_items_rendered_v1.csv
# 2.5 MB, but it cost five jobs to produce. Published to HuggingFace.
# Regenerate: sbatch/run_exec_trajectories.sbatch
data/exec_trajectories.npz

# Delivered source data. NOT regenerable -- kept out of git for size and published
# to HuggingFace instead. md5 b9f5f332176bae894a061c9f2f5e64e0.
data/multimodality_physics_with_trajectories.csv

# Exact duplicate of the file above, under a browser-default name. Verified
# byte-identical (same md5). Safe to delete; ignored so it cannot be committed.
comma-separated values.csv

# Result CSVs -- rebuilt from the published HF datasets by viz/refresh_report.sh
results/*.csv
results/xmodal/
results/xmodal_summary.json
results/xmodal_summary.csv
# Raw per-model generation JSONL. Same reasoning as results/xmodal/ above: every arm
# is published to HuggingFace (pde-llm-eval-freegen-xmodal-<slug>) and mirrored at
# /scratch/ehb7466/projects/pde-llm-eval/outputs/, so git would be a third copy of
# 100+ MB that nothing reads from.
results/freegen_xmodal/
results/xmodal_glm/
results/xmodal_glm_summary.json

# Generated reports: multi-MB and self-contained, republished by refresh_report.sh
viz/pde_dual_report.html
viz/*_report.html
